CREATED:20260527T143051Z
DESCRIPTION:On November 6th and 7th\, AGS will be taking a group of studen
 ts and alumni to the National World War II Museum in New Orleans\, Louisi
 ana. Our visit will include tours of the museum's galleries\, expert brie
 fings\, and the museum's featured 4D film.\nThe group will depart on an e
 arly morning flight on Friday\, November 6\, and return on the night of S
 aturday\, November 7. All applicants are expected to be available during 
 the full duration of the trip and to actively participate in all meetings
  and events.\n\nAGS will cover airfare\, lodging\, lunches\, dinner on Fr
 iday\, and any entry fees as needed.\n\nTransportation to/from Raleigh-Du
 rham International Airport and any additional meals or personal incidenta
 ls are at the individual's expense.\nPlease complete your application no 
 later than September 24th for consideration. \nAll Duke undergraduate and
  graduate students are encouraged to apply\, regardless of program of stu
 dy\, year\, or prior involvement with AGS\, no specific expertise or expe
 rience is required.
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T220000
