DESCRIPTION:The colloquium meets every three semesters and brings together
  faculty\, PhD students\, and postdocs from Berkeley\, Stanford\, Princet
 on\, Toronto\, and the Carolina-Duke Graduate Program in German Studies\,
  which is hosting for the first time this year\, co-sponsored by Duke's P
 rogram in Medieval and Renaissance Studies. The colloquium runs from 9:00
  am to 5:00 pm at UNC on November 6 (in Toy Lounge\, Dey Hall) and Novemb
 er 7 (Incubator Room\, Hyde Hall). The event is open to the public\, and 
 pre-circulated papers being presented by the graduate students may be obt
 ained from Dr. Aleksandra Prica at aprica@email.unc.edu. The full program
  may be seen by clicking More Information.
DURATION:PT8H
