CREATED:20260714T174749Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the Duke Chinese Music Ensemble for an evening of musical
  storytelling that journeys from the silver screen to the rich traditions
  of Chinese folk music. Bringing together beloved melodies from Chinese t
 elevision dramas\, Japanese animated films\, and traditional works\, this
  concert explores how music brings stories\, emotions\, and cultural trad
 itions to life.\n\nThe program features iconic themes from classic Hong K
 ong martial arts dramas\, including The Legend of the Condor Heroes and L
 u Xiaofeng\, alongside memorable selections from Studio Ghibli's Princess
  Mononoke and Spirited Away. Audiences will also experience the poignant 
 melodies of Dream of the Red Chamber and selections from The Butterfly Lo
 vers\, a timeless Chinese love story often compared to Romeo and Juliet.\
 n\nBeyond the screen\, the ensemble celebrates the vibrant traditions of 
 Chinese folk music with pieces that evoke galloping horses across the gra
 sslands of Inner Mongolia\, playful exchanges between village characters\
 , and the rhythmic sounds of walnuts rolling across rooftops during harve
 st season.\n\nFeaturing guest vocalist Ying Wang\, instrumental soloists\
 , chamber performances\, and the full ensemble\, the concert brings toget
 her traditional Chinese and Western instruments to create a colorful musi
 cal experience.\n\nFrom sweeping cinematic melodies to spirited folk trad
 itions\, discover the stories that music can tell-no words required.\n\nT
 his event is free and open to the public. All are welcome.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20261027T172614Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T170000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T172614Z
