CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a0183a7-83184018-0184-f88b4dd1-00001a24:Franklin\,
  Monica
CREATED:20230805T023014Z
DESCRIPTION:Behavior is the ultimate output of the nervous system\, but it
  has long resisted precise measurement. My lab develops AI tools\, includ
 ing SLEAP\, that extract detailed body kinematics from video at scale\, t
 urning behavior into quantitative data on par with neural recordings and 
 connectomes. We then use these measurements to build embodied neuromechan
 ical models: artificial neural networks that control physically simulated
  animal bodies\, linking neural circuits\, biomechanics\, and behavior in
  a single framework. Because these models are generative\, they can simul
 ate perturbations and produce mechanistic hypotheses that can be tested d
 irectly at the bench\, creating a feedback loop between AI and experiment
 al neuroscience.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261104T000237Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T120000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261104T000237Z
LOCATION;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf6e-00000000:None
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Embodied Neuromechanics or: How I Learned to Stop Worrying and Lov
 e NeuroAI
