DESCRIPTION:Join Duke University's Nicholas School of the Environment and 
 Villa Albertine\, the French Embassy's Mission for Culture and Education\
 , for a panel discussion exploring how environmental policymaking has evo
 lved over the past decade\, the role of social movements and what these c
 hanges mean for challenges such as climate change. Cosponsored by the Duk
 e Center for French & Francophone Studies.\nReception to follow.
