CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20261020T224504Z
DESCRIPTION:As ice cream consumption increases\, so do shark attacks\, but
  does eating ice cream really cause shark attacks? This example shows how
  two things can be related without one causing the other. Yet\, in resear
 ch\, figuring out whether we can make a causal claim about the relationsh
 ip between two variables isn't always so simple. This workshop introduces
  the basics of causal inference and helps you think more carefully about 
 the claims you make as a researcher.\n\nBy the end of the workshop\, you'
 ll have a better understanding of how to:\n~Identify what's needed to est
 ablish causality.\n~Explore simple experimental and quasi-experimental ap
 proaches to studying cause and effect.\n~Develop your own causal research
  questions.\n\nIf you want to move beyond identifying relationships and s
 tart exploring cause and effect\, join us for this workshop.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261020T225748Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261109T170000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261020T225748Z
