CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a000483-92c3adf6-0193-9d66c697-00004589:McManus-Vi
 ana\, Kayla
X-BEDEWORK-COST:Free!
CREATED:20261014T162656Z
DESCRIPTION:This talk interrogates how slavery animates the psychic counte
 rs of abortion concerns. From the use of the Civil War as a metaphor for 
 battles over personhood by abortion legal scholars such as Mary Ziegler t
 o the constitutional originalism espoused by Justice Samuel Alito's readi
 ng of the fourteenth amendment in Dobbs\, slavery occupies a foundational
  psychic landscape with the rhetorical strategies of abortion battles. To
  trace this emergence\, this talk returns to nineteenth century medical j
 urisprudence to consider how the concept of portio viscerum matris situat
 es gestation as the dividing line between the status of life and the cond
 itions of property.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20261025T234252Z
